# 必考词 Unit01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit01核心高频词汇

{{abandon}}{/əˈbændən/}{{v. 放弃；抛弃；n. 放纵}}{{He abandoned his plan to study abroad due to financial difficulties.}}

{{abstract}}{/ˈæbstrækt/}{{adj. 抽象的；n. 摘要}}{{The professor asked us to write an abstract of the research paper.}}

{{absorb}}{/əbˈzɔːrb/}{{v. 吸收；吸引；使全神贯注}}{{The sponge can absorb a large amount of water.}}

{{abuse}}{/əˈbjuːz/}{{v./n. 滥用；虐待；辱骂}}{{The law aims to protect children from abuse.}}

{{academic}}{/ˌækəˈdemɪk/}{{adj. 学术的；学院的}}{{She pursued an academic career in linguistics.}}

{{accelerate}}{/əkˈseləreɪt/}{{v. 加速；促进}}{{The government decided to accelerate economic reforms.}}

{{access}}{/ˈækses/}{{n. 进入；通道；v. 访问}}{{All students have access to the university library.}}

{{accommodate}}{/əˈkɒmədeɪt/}{{v. 容纳；提供住宿；适应}}{{The hotel can accommodate up to 500 guests.}}

{{accompany}}{/əˈkʌmpəni/}{{v. 陪伴；伴随}}{{Lightning is often accompanied by thunder.}}

{{accomplish}}{/əˈkʌmplɪʃ/}{{v. 完成；实现}}{{She accomplished her goal of running a marathon.}}

{{account}}{/əˈkaʊnt/}{{n. 账户；描述；v. 解释}}{{He opened a savings account at the bank.}}

{{accumulate}}{/əˈkjuːmjəleɪt/}{{v. 积累；堆积}}{{Dust accumulates quickly on the bookshelf.}}

{{accurate}}{/ˈækjərət/}{{adj. 准确的；精确的}}{{The report provides an accurate description of the situation.}}

{{accuse}}{/əˈkjuːz/}{{v. 指控；谴责}}{{He was accused of stealing the confidential data.}}

{{achieve}}{/əˈtʃiːv/}{{v. 达到；取得}}{{Hard work is essential to achieve success.}}

{{acknowledge}}{/əkˈnɒlɪdʒ/}{{v. 承认；致谢}}{{She acknowledged that she had made a mistake.}}

{{acquire}}{/əˈkwaɪər/}{{v. 获得；学到}}{{He acquired a deep knowledge of history through years of study.}}

{{adapt}}{/əˈdæpt/}{{v. 适应；改编}}{{It takes time to adapt to a new environment.}}

{{adequate}}{/ˈædɪkwət/}{{adj. 足够的；适当的}}{{The supply of food is adequate for the refugees.}}

{{adjust}}{/əˈdʒʌst/}{{v. 调整；适应}}{{You need to adjust the mirror before driving.}}

{{administration}}{/ədˌmɪnɪˈstreɪʃn/}{{n. 管理；行政}}{{The administration of the company is very efficient.}}

{{admire}}{/ədˈmaɪər/}{{v. 钦佩；欣赏}}{{I admire her courage in facing difficulties.}}

{{adopt}}{/əˈdɒpt/}{{v. 采用；收养}}{{The company adopted a new strategy to increase sales.}}

{{advance}}{/ədˈvɑːns/}{{v./n. 前进；进步}}{{Technology continues to advance at a rapid pace.}}

{{advantage}}{/ədˈvɑːntɪdʒ/{{n. 优势；有利条件}}{{Being bilingual is a great advantage in the job market.}}

{{advocate}}{/ˈædvəkeɪt/}{{v. 提倡；n. 倡导者}}{{Many scientists advocate for renewable energy.}}

{{affect}}{/əˈfekt/}{{v. 影响；感动}}{{The weather can affect our mood significantly.}}

{{afford}}{/əˈfɔːrd/}{{v. 负担得起；提供}}{{Many families cannot afford to buy a house in the city.}}

{{agenda}}{/əˈdʒendə/}{{n. 议程；日程安排}}{{The agenda for tomorrow's meeting has been set.}}

{{aggressive}}{/əˈɡresɪv/}{{adj. 侵略性的；有进取心的}}{{The company adopted an aggressive marketing strategy.}}

{{alert}}{/əˈlɜːrt/}{{adj. 警觉的；v. 使警觉}}{{The guard remained alert throughout the night.}}

{{allocate}}{/ˈæləkeɪt/}{{v. 分配；拨出}}{{The government allocated funds for education reform.}}

{{alter}}{/ˈɔːltər/}{{v. 改变；修改}}{{They had to alter the plan due to bad weather.}}

{{alternative}}{/ɔːlˈtɜːrnətɪv/}{{n. 替代选择；adj. 可替代的}}{{We need to find an alternative solution to this problem.}}

{{amateur}}{/ˈæmətər/}{{n. 业余爱好者；adj. 业余的}}{{The photography competition was open to both amateurs and professionals.}}

{{ambitious}}{/æmˈbɪʃəs/}{{adj. 有雄心的；野心勃勃的}}{{She is an ambitious young woman who wants to change the world.}}

{{amend}}{/əˈmend/}{{v. 修正；改进}}{{The parliament voted to amend the constitution.}}

{{ample}}{/ˈæmpl/}{{adj. 充足的；丰富的}}{{There is ample evidence to support the theory.}}

{{analyse/analyze}}{/ˈænəlaɪz/}{{v. 分析}}{{Scientists analysed the data from the experiment carefully.}}

{{ancient}}{/ˈeɪnʃənt/}{{adj. 古代的；古老的}}{{The ancient civilization left behind many magnificent ruins.}}
